<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help: </ansi><ansi fg="command">Special Moves & Cooldown</ansi>

Several combat abilities are considered <ansi fg="yellow-bold">special moves</ansi> and share a common
cooldown. Triggering any one of them puts all of them on cooldown for the
same window.

<ansi fg="yellow">Special moves that share this cooldown:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">grapple</ansi>
              - Melee control moves: stagger, disorient, knock down, restrain.
  <ansi fg="command">taunt</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">warcry</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">rally</ansi>
              - Shouts and rallying cries — the voice spends from the
                same well of focus.
  <ansi fg="command">cast</ansi>      - Initiates spellcasting. Counts as a special move on
              initiation.
  <ansi fg="command">reload</ansi>    - Working a ranged weapon's mechanism takes the same
              burst of focus.
  <ansi fg="command">gore</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">maul</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">rake</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">pounce</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">throttle</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">hamstring</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">drain</ansi>
              - Natural-weapon moves for bodies shaped to use them.
  Mutation abilities (<ansi fg="command">venom-coat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">cocoon</ansi>) share it too.

Submissions (chokes, joint locks) fire automatically when you
have dominant control in a grapple — no command needed. See
<ansi fg="command">help submission</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Why shared cooldown?</ansi>

These moves represent bursts of focused effort — the body and mind need a
moment to recover before another such effort can be made. You can still
attack normally between special moves.

<ansi fg="yellow">Checking cooldowns:</ansi>

  Use <ansi fg="command">cooldowns</ansi> to see all active cooldowns, including how many rounds
  remain before your next special move is available.

